WEBVTT


00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.560
If you happen to run across one of these
interesting little tools, you might

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.030
scratch your head at first.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.710
What is it?

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.960
This double ended latched tool is
also known as the seed stitch tool.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.480
Now, seed stitch in the US consists of
alternating knit and purl stitches across

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.450
each row and alternating rows.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.410
I understand this is called Moss
stitch and other parts of the world.

00:00:26.895 --> 00:00:31.365
If you don't use a Brother G-carriage,
anytime machine knitters attempt to

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:35.355
combine, knit and purl stitches
means hand manipulation.

00:00:36.665 --> 00:00:40.275
This tool can help to use it.

00:00:40.345 --> 00:00:41.735
Drop a single stitch.

00:00:55.224 --> 00:01:01.045
Insert the tool in the first
stitch and reform the first stitch.

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:08.824
Next, push the tools so the stitch
rests on the opposite end of the tool.

00:01:09.585 --> 00:01:14.744
And use the hook on this end to catch
the next strand in the ladder and form a

00:01:14.744 --> 00:01:16.335
stitch in the opposite direction.

00:01:17.295 --> 00:01:21.925
Continue up the ladder, back and forth,
back and forth, creating alternate knit

00:01:22.024 --> 00:01:23.205
and purl stitches.

00:01:24.975 --> 00:01:29.324
You'll repeat this across the entire area
of seed stitch that you want to work.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.730
Now you might find it easier to remove the
work from the machine onto waste yarn and

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.640
then reform the stitches off the machine.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.740
Try it both ways.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.480
See which is easier for you.

00:01:50.139 --> 00:01:54.210
I don't know about you, but I certainly
don't have the patience to create large

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.449
amounts of seed stitch.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:00.359
I'll pick up my hand knitting needles
first, but a little bit of seeds ditch

00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:04.949
here and there may just be the designer
touch you're looking for, and this little

00:02:04.949 --> 00:02:07.589
tool is a boon for getting that done.

